  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/37674375730f32a70d7909a7ab01f3f9c836cf9c72d16447d499af20427f022c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z\u223cN(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=\u03a6(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>-0.97).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/a8b07524ca3a1ac1750f86e9a5088a07150d7d1b038158e74d924b8811a405a0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<0.97).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ef497f11f5ec451215e923157b6675d16c175dc23ec7d6576bf0a018e3ef594c.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>-0.97)=P(Z<0.97)=\u03a6(0.97)=0.8340.\n$$",
